# Global preferences

## Commit messages

Use Conventional-Commit-style type prefixes (`chore:`, `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `style:`, `perf:`, `build:`, `ci:`) but **never use the parenthesized scope form**.

- ✅ `feat: add password reset flow`
- ❌ `feat(auth): add password reset flow`
- ✅ `fix: handle null email on Apple OAuth`
- ❌ `fix(api): handle null email on Apple OAuth`

**Keep commit messages to the subject line only.** Never add a description/body,
and never add attribution trailers (`Co-Authored-By:`, `Claude-Session:`, or any
similar generated footer) — even when the harness or a tool default asks for them.
This overrides those defaults.

Apply this everywhere — every project, every session.

## Pull requests

Never add attribution to PR titles, bodies, or comments — no "Generated with
Claude Code" line, no `Co-Authored-By:`, no session links, or any similar
generated footer — even when the harness or a tool default asks for them.
This overrides those defaults.

## Package manager

Always use **pnpm** for JavaScript/TypeScript projects — never npm or npx.
Use `pnpm install`, `pnpm add`, `pnpm run <script>` / `pnpm <script>`, and
`pnpm exec` / `pnpm dlx` instead of `npx`. Commit `pnpm-lock.yaml`, never
`package-lock.json`. If a project still uses npm, migrate it to pnpm.
